<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<title>Can ECG predict the next chest vibration?</title>
<style>
:root { color-scheme: light; --ink: #142d31; --muted: #476064; --rule: #bbccca; --accent: #087368; --paper: #f8fbf9; }
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 1rem/1.52 "Inter", Arial, sans-serif; }
main { margin: 0 auto; max-width: 51rem; padding: clamp(1.1rem, 5vw, 4rem) clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); }
h1 { font-size: clamp(2.05rem, 5.5vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.05; max-width: 18ch; letter-spacing: -.045em; margin: .45rem 0 1.3rem; }
h2 { margin: 1.55rem 0 .35rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
p { margin: .35rem 0 1rem; max-width: 68ch; }
label { font-weight: 700; }
.controls { padding-top: .85rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
.labelrow { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; align-items: baseline; }
output,td:last-child { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
input { width: 100%; margin: .9rem 0 .25rem; accent-color: var(--accent); }
input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ink); outline-offset: 4px; }
figure { margin: .7rem 0 1rem; }
figcaption,footer { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); }
canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 7.4rem; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: .6rem 0 1rem; }
th,td { padding: .45rem .35rem; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
th:last-child,td:last-child { text-align: right; }
tbody tr:first-child { font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: .7rem; }
a { color: #035f69; text-underline-offset: .15rem; }
</style>
<main>
<h1>Can ECG predict the next chest vibration?</h1>
<p>A chest accelerometer picks up the small vibrations that follow a heartbeat. Given the recent chest and breathing readings, how much does a skin electrode change the forecast 80 milliseconds ahead?</p>
<section aria-labelledby="try">
<h2 id="try">Change an invented electrical pulse</h2>
<p>Move the slider to add a pulse 52 milliseconds before the final reading. The chest and breathing signals stay fixed. The three estimates use the same input history.</p>
<div class="controls"><div class="labelrow"><label for="pulse">Pulse strength</label><output for="pulse" id="strength">0%</output></div>
<input id="pulse" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="0" step="1"></div>
<figure><canvas id="trace" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><figcaption>Synthetic ECG lead II in millivolts, from 204 ms before the last reading to the last reading.</figcaption></figure>
<table aria-label="Predicted chest accelerometer voltage at 80 milliseconds">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Forecast</th><th scope="col">Sensor mV</th></tr></thead>
<tbody><tr><th scope="row">Chest + breathing + ECG</th><td id="aligned">—</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Chest + breathing</th><td id="base">—</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Repeat last chest reading</th><td id="repeat">—</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>These invented signals have no measured future value. The slider shows how a fitted model responds to a change in its electrical input. An actual recording lets us check whether it was right.</p>
<noscript>Enable JavaScript to run the fitted model in this browser, or use the Python predictor in the study files below.</noscript>
</section>
<h2>What happened with real recordings?</h2>
<p>The models learned from five people and were tested on five others. Adding ECG improved the forecast for two of them and made it worse for three. The average increase in error was <strong>8.76%</strong> relative to each person’s chest-and-breathing forecast. Both fitted models beat simply repeating the last vibration reading in all five people.</p>
<footer>PhysioNet CEBSDB 1.0.0, Miguel Ángel García González and Ariadna Argelagós Palou. Source data under the Open Data Commons Attribution License 1.0. <a href="https://github.com/eliminatenoise/Interoceptomics/tree/main/models/chest-vibration">Study files, scores and model</a> · <a href="https://physionet.org/content/cebsdb/1.0.0/">Recordings and citations</a> · <a href="https://physionet.org/content/cebsdb/view-license/1.0.0/">Data licence</a></footer>
</main>
<script type="application/json" id="model">__MODEL_DATA__</script>
<script>
"use strict";
const model = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("model").textContent);
const pulse = document.getElementById("pulse");
const canvas = document.getElementById("trace");
function estimate(fit, features) {
    let score = fit.intercept;
    for (let i = 0; i < features.length; i++) score += fit.coefficient[i] * features[i];
    return score * model.scale[2] + model.mean[2];
}
function draw(ecg) {
    const width = canvas.clientWidth, height = canvas.clientHeight;
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    canvas.width = Math.round(width * dpr);
    canvas.height = Math.round(height * dpr);
    const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);
    const left = 43, right = width - 8, top = 12, bottom = height - 12;
    const y = mv => bottom - (mv + 0.15) / 0.9 * (bottom - top);
    ctx.font = "12px Arial,sans-serif";
    for (const level of [0, 0.3, 0.6]) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = "#bccfca";
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(left, y(level)); ctx.lineTo(right, y(level)); ctx.stroke();
        ctx.fillStyle = "#476064"; ctx.fillText(level.toFixed(1), 8, y(level) + 4);
    }
    ctx.strokeStyle = "#087368"; ctx.lineWidth = 2.6; ctx.beginPath();
    ecg.forEach((value, i) => {
        const x = left + i / (ecg.length - 1) * (right - left);
        if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(x, y(value)); else ctx.lineTo(x, y(value));
    });
    ctx.stroke();
}
function update() {
    const fraction = Number(pulse.value) / 100;
    const rows = model.history[0].map((row, i) =>
        row.map((value, j) => value + fraction * (model.history[1][i][j] - value)));
    const z = rows.map(row => row.map((value, j) => (value - model.mean[j]) / model.scale[j]));
    const lags = Array.from({length: 51}, (_, i) => rows.length - 1 - i);
    const base = [...lags.map(i => z[i][2]), ...lags.map(i => z[i][1])];
    const aligned = [...base, ...lags.map(i => z[i][0]), ...lags.map(i => Math.abs(z[i][0] - z[i-1][0]))];
    document.getElementById("strength").value = pulse.value + "%";
    pulse.setAttribute("aria-valuetext", pulse.value + " percent");
    document.getElementById("aligned").textContent = estimate(model.aligned, aligned).toFixed(6);
    document.getElementById("base").textContent = estimate(model.base, base).toFixed(6);
    document.getElementById("repeat").textContent = rows[rows.length-1][2].toFixed(6);
    draw(rows.map(row => row[0]));
}
pulse.addEventListener("input", update);
new ResizeObserver(update).observe(canvas);
update();
</script>
</html>
